+## Continuous integration
+
+GitHub Actions runs the pipeline in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` on every push to `main`, on every pull request, and on demand (**Actions** tab, workflow **CI**, **Run workflow**). The jobs run in parallel:
+
+| Job | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| Static analysis | Backend: Ruff (lint, import order, complexity and security rules), Bandit (security scan) and mypy (type checking). Frontend: ESLint |
+| Backend tests (Python 3.12 and 3.13) | Unit tests, then integration tests against the MariaDB container loaded with `data/addresses.sql`, then a coverage report. The job fails if the coverage is below 90% |
+| API tests (Postman) | Starts the API and runs the Postman collection with the Postman CLI |
+| E2E tests (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit) | Starts the API and the frontend and runs the Playwright tests, one job per browser |
+
+The workflow `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` runs GitHub's CodeQL analysis for Python and JavaScript on every push and pull request to `main`, and weekly. The findings are shown under **Security**, **Code scanning**.
+
+The coverage report (`coverage-python-*`) and the Playwright reports (`playwright-report-*`) are saved as artifacts of each run. The pipeline starts the database the same way as this README: with `backend/compose.yaml`, followed by the import of `data/addresses.sql`.
+
+The static analysis can be run locally with the same commands:
+
+```
+cd backend
+uv run ruff check .
+uv run bandit -c pyproject.toml -r app
+uv run mypy
+```
+
+and `npm run lint` in the `frontend` folder. The settings are in `backend/pyproject.toml`.
